models/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.safetensors
eval/fixtures/*.txt
!eval/fixtures/*.key.json

# build/ holds the artifacts that DEFINE the model, and they total 17 MB.
# Ignoring them left the eval reproducible but the build not: nobody could see
# which experts this model kept, or check the arithmetic behind that choice.
#
# survey.saliency.npz is the expensive one -- the tagged calibration run, hours
# of compute. Committing it means any arm (reference mix, hr-only, hr-heavy)
# can be derived with reap_subset.py without recalibrating, which is the
# "calibrate once, subset many" property the whole design rests on.
